{\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b 4.\tab}
\pard\ssparaaux0\s0\tx720\ls1\ilvl0\fi-360\li720\ql\widctlpar\plain\f0\fs22\plain\f2\fs22 Enter the last four digits of your Social Security Number (xxxx) and Date of Birth (mm/dd/yyyy) as indicated and click\plain\f2\fs22\lang1033\hich\f2\dbch\f2\loch\f2\cf5\fs22 
 \plain\f2\fs22\lang1033\hich\f2\dbch\f2\loch\f2\cf2\fs22\b Next\plain\f2\fs22 . You will be taken to the next sign-up page.\par 
{\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b 5.\tab}
Create a MyUnityPoint ID. This will be your MyUnityPoint login ID and cannot be changed, so think of one that is secure and easy to remember.\par 
{\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b 6.\tab}
Create a MyUnityPoint password. You can change your password at any time.\par 
{\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b 7.\tab}
Enter your Password Reset Question and Answer and click \plain\f2\fs22\lang1033\hich\f2\dbch\f2\loch\f2\fs22\b Next\plain\f2\fs22 . This can be used at a later time if you forget your password. \par 
{\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b 8.\tab}
Select your communication preference, and if applicable enter your e-mail address. You will receive e-mail notification when new information is available in MyUnityPoint by choosing to receive e-mail notifications and filling in your e-mail.\par 
{\listtext\pard\plain\f2\fs22\b 9.\tab}
Click \plain\f2\fs22\lang1033\hich\f2\dbch\f2\loch\f2\fs22\b Sign In\plain\f2\fs22 . You can now view your medical record.\par 
